the market situation of course was the  main issue again just like the last five  councils we had it has dominated our  council meetings during our presidency  and still the situation in several  agricultural sectors especially the  dairy pig meat and fruit and vegetable  sectors continues to be worrisome today  the Commission has given an update on  price developments and on the  implementation of the support measures  taken we concluded although some of the  price developments we're heading in a  positive direction slowly we had to  conclude that most of the farm incomes  are still negatively affected by the  ongoing market situation and also our  economies they're all depending on a  strong and healthy agriculture so they  face difficulties because of that market  situation and we agreed that the  difficult situation is calling for  additional measures the council  concluded that an additional financial  package should be agreed upon as soon as  possible and it urged the Commission to  present an additional package in the  council of July and later on the  Commissioner Hogan stated that a  proposal will be on the table next July  at a council called on the Commission to  table a proposal that would include  measures to stabilize or structurally  reduce production in the dairy sector  financial support measures from member  states to restructure the dairy or pig  meat sectors or to structurally reduce  supply and with that giving the  flexibility to member states to target a  to either sector and to add specific  conditions like limiting support for  businesses that face liquidity problems  specific conditions that fits specific  circumstances in the Member States
 

